2.
Definitions.
- In these rules, unless the context otherwise requires,-
(a)
"Act" means the Insurance Act, 1938 (
4 of 1938
);
(b)
"adjudicating officer" means the officer appointed by the Authority as adjudicating officer under sub-section (1) of section
105 C of the Act;
(c)
"Authority" means the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India established under sub-section (1) of
section 3 of the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority Act, 1999 (
41 of 1999
);
(d)
"Inquiry" means the inquiry referred in section 105C of the Act;
(e)
"section" means section of the Act;
(f)
all other words and expressions used in these rules but not defined and defined in the Act shall have the meanings
respectively assigned to them in the Act.
